# Vergence release signers, in ssh-keygen allowed_signers format.
#
# PLACEHOLDER: Vergence has no releases yet, so no key is pinned and the updater (off by
# default) can verify nothing. When releases start:
#   - sign each release's SHA256SUMS with `ssh-keygen -Y sign -n vergence-release`;
#   - pin the signing key and an offline backup here, both from the first release that ships
#     this file (a backup added later is worthless: nothing installed would trust it);
#   - set `updater::SITE` to the site serving release.json.
#
# The structure is Apparition's (MIT, same author): its desktop updater and release manifest
# verification, adapted. Lines look like:
# releases@example.invalid ssh-ed25519 AAAA...
